node_modules/
dist/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# A GitHub App private key IS the App: whoever holds it can act as it on every
# repository the App is installed on. One landed at the repository root during setup,
# untracked but not ignored — a single `git add -A` from being public. The key itself
# belongs outside the repository (`~/.config/test-framework-v2/github-app.pem`); this
# is the net under that, not the plan.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# The evidence store. Content-addressed blobs of agent transcripts and captured test
# output — whatever an agent read out of a repository ends up here. It appeared untracked
# and unignored after the first real run, 672K and one `git add -A` from a commit. It is
# a run's evidence, not source, and `ENGINE_BLOB_ROOT` can point anywhere.
.blobs/
# The same thing, for the two programs milestone 9 added: a plane holds what runners
# upload, and a runner holds what its containers produce before they are shipped.
.plane-blobs/
.runner-blobs/
*.log
.DS_Store
.neon
